msgid "Export and deletion"
msgstr "Export et suppression"

msgid "The data of a home belongs to its owners, who can take it out and delete it; the data of a person is erased with their account ([ADR 0023](../adr/0023-audit-log-export-erasure-and-email-alerts.md)). The administrator of the instance does neither for a home they do not own."
msgstr "Les données d'un logement appartiennent à ses propriétaires, qui peuvent les récupérer et les supprimer ; les données d'une personne sont effacées avec son compte ([ADR 0023](../adr/0023-audit-log-export-erasure-and-email-alerts.md)). L'administrateur de l'instance ne fait ni l'un ni l'autre pour un logement dont il n'est pas propriétaire."

msgid "Export of a home"
msgstr "Export d'un logement"

msgid "An owner downloads the archive from the page of the home (**Export all data**) or from the API (`POST /api/v1/homes/<id>/export/`, signed in; an API token cannot). The export is written to the audit log of the home."
msgstr "Un propriétaire télécharge l'archive depuis la page du logement (**Exporter toutes les données**) ou depuis l'API (`POST /api/v1/homes/<id>/export/`, connecté ; un jeton d'API ne peut pas). L'export est inscrit au journal d'audit du logement."

msgid "The archive is a zip:"
msgstr "L'archive est un fichier zip :"

msgid "Part"
msgstr "Élément"

msgid "Content"
msgstr "Contenu"

msgid "`export.json`"
msgstr "`export.json`"

msgid "The data, as JSON (below)."
msgstr "Les données, au format JSON (ci-dessous)."

msgid "`files/`"
msgstr "`files/`"

msgid "The files of the home, at the paths `export.json` lists: the photos, under `files/photos/`, the files of the tasks, under `files/attachments/`, the photos of the labels of stock items, under `files/stock/`, the photos and quote files of projects, under `files/projects/`, and the photos of the reports, under `files/reports/`."
msgstr "Les fichiers du logement, aux chemins que liste `export.json` : les photos, sous `files/photos/`, les fichiers des tâches, sous `files/attachments/`, les photos d'étiquettes des articles du matériel, sous `files/stock/`, les photos et fichiers de devis des projets, sous `files/projects/`, et les photos des signalements, sous `files/reports/`."

msgid "`README.txt`"
msgstr "`README.txt`"

msgid "A reminder of the format."
msgstr "Un rappel du format."

msgid "`export.json` is versioned. Version `1` has these keys:"
msgstr "`export.json` est versionné. La version `1` comporte ces clés :"

msgid "Key"
msgstr "Clé"

msgid "`format`, `version`"
msgstr "`format`, `version`"

msgid "`\"housecairn-export\"` and `1`. A change that removes or renames a key raises the version."
msgstr "`\"housecairn-export\"` et `1`. Un changement qui supprime ou renomme une clé augmente la version."

msgid "`exported_at`, `application_version`"
msgstr "`exported_at`, `application_version`"

msgid "When, and by which version."
msgstr "Quand, et par quelle version."

msgid "`home`"
msgstr "`home`"

msgid "`id`, `name`, `currency`, `hemisphere` (`north` or `south`), `required_provider`, `created_at`."
msgstr "`id`, `name`, `currency`, `hemisphere` (`north` ou `south`), `required_provider`, `created_at`."

msgid "`members`"
msgstr "`members`"

msgid "`id`, `email`, `name` (the display name, else the full name, else the part of the address before the `@`), `role`, `joined_at` of each member."
msgstr "`id`, `email`, `name` (le nom d'affichage, sinon le nom complet, sinon la partie de l'adresse avant le `@`), `role`, `joined_at` de chaque membre."

msgid "`pending_invitations`"
msgstr "`pending_invitations`"

msgid "`id`, `email`, `role`, `sent_at`, `expires_at`; never a link."
msgstr "`id`, `email`, `role`, `sent_at`, `expires_at` ; jamais de lien."

msgid "`events`"
msgstr "`events`"

msgid "`id`, `kind`, `payload`, `received_at` of the events received."
msgstr "`id`, `kind`, `payload`, `received_at` des événements reçus."

msgid "`rooms`"
msgstr "`rooms`"

msgid "`id`, `name`, `kind`, `position`, `notes`, `created_at` of each room, and its `memory` (paint colour, brand, reference, batch, `paint_article` (a stock item id or `null`), floor and wall covering, memory notes)."
msgstr "`id`, `name`, `kind`, `position`, `notes`, `created_at` de chaque pièce, et sa `memory` (couleur, marque, référence et lot de la peinture, `paint_article` (l'identifiant d'un article ou `null`), revêtement de sol et de mur, notes de mémoire)."

msgid "`items`"
msgstr "`items`"

msgid "`id`, `room`, `name`, `kind`, `brand`, `model`, `serial_number`, `installed_on`, `warranty_ends_on`, `contract_provider`, `contract_number`, `contract_url`, `links`, `notes`, `created_at` of each item."
msgstr "`id`, `room`, `name`, `kind`, `brand`, `model`, `serial_number`, `installed_on`, `warranty_ends_on`, `contract_provider`, `contract_number`, `contract_url`, `links`, `notes`, `created_at` de chaque élément."

msgid "`photos`"
msgstr "`photos`"

msgid "`id`, `room` or `item`, `category`, `caption`, `content_type`, `size_bytes`, `width`, `height`, `created_at`, and `file`, the path of the photo in the archive (`files/photos/<id>.<extension>`, or `null` if the file is missing)."
msgstr "`id`, `room` ou `item`, `category`, `caption`, `content_type`, `size_bytes`, `width`, `height`, `created_at`, et `file`, le chemin de la photo dans l'archive (`files/photos/<id>.<extension>`, ou `null` si le fichier manque)."

msgid "`attachments`"
msgstr "`attachments`"

msgid "`id`, `task`, `occurrence` or `null`, `name`, `content_type`, `is_image`, `size_bytes`, `width`, `height`, `created_at`, and `file`, the path of the file in the archive (`files/attachments/<id>.<extension>`, or `null` if the file is missing)."
msgstr "`id`, `task`, `occurrence` ou `null`, `name`, `content_type`, `is_image`, `size_bytes`, `width`, `height`, `created_at`, et `file`, le chemin du fichier dans l'archive (`files/attachments/<id>.<extension>`, ou `null` si le fichier manque)."

msgid "`stock_items`"
msgstr "`stock_items`"

msgid "`id`, `name`, `manufacturer_reference`, `dimensions`, `storage_location`, `unit` (a code of the list, or `other`), `unit_other`, `threshold`, `quantity`, `compatible_items` (item ids), `rooms` (room ids), `notes`, `created_at`, and `label`, the path of the photo of the label in the archive (`files/stock/<id>.<extension>`, or `null`)."
msgstr "`id`, `name`, `manufacturer_reference`, `dimensions`, `storage_location`, `unit` (un code de la liste, ou `other`), `unit_other`, `threshold`, `quantity`, `compatible_items` (identifiants d'éléments), `rooms` (identifiants de pièces), `notes`, `created_at`, et `label`, le chemin de la photo de l'étiquette dans l'archive (`files/stock/<id>.<extension>`, ou `null`)."

msgid "`stock_suppliers`"
msgstr "`stock_suppliers`"

msgid "`id`, `article`, `name`, `reference`, `url`, `last_price`, `created_at`."
msgstr "`id`, `article`, `name`, `reference`, `url`, `last_price`, `created_at`."

msgid "`stock_movements`"
msgstr "`stock_movements`"

msgid "`id`, `article`, `kind`, `quantity`, `delta`, `occurred_on`, `note`, `occurrence` (the occurrence of a task whose closing wrote the line, or `null`), `created_at`."
msgstr "`id`, `article`, `kind`, `quantity`, `delta`, `occurred_on`, `note`, `occurrence` (l'occurrence d'une tâche dont la clôture a écrit la ligne, ou `null`), `created_at`."

msgid "`task_materials`"
msgstr "`task_materials`"

msgid "`id`, `task`, `article`, `quantity`, `created_at`: the stock items each task needs."
msgstr "`id`, `task`, `article`, `quantity`, `created_at` : les articles dont chaque tâche a besoin."

msgid "`stock_draws`"
msgstr "`stock_draws`"

msgid "`id`, `occurrence`, `article`, `wanted`, `drawn`, `created_at`: what each closed occurrence took from the stock."
msgstr "`id`, `occurrence`, `article`, `wanted`, `drawn`, `created_at` : ce que chaque occurrence close a pris dans le stock."

msgid "`projects`"
msgstr "`projects`"

msgid "`id`, `title`, `goal`, `status`, `priority`, `rooms` (room ids), `estimated_minutes`, `season` with `season_start_month` and `season_end_month`, `created_at`."
msgstr "`id`, `title`, `goal`, `status`, `priority`, `rooms` (identifiants de pièces), `estimated_minutes`, `season` avec `season_start_month` et `season_end_month`, `created_at`."

msgid "`project_budget_lines`"
msgstr "`project_budget_lines`"

msgid "`id`, `project`, `label`, `nature`, `planned`, `committed` (the sum of the accepted quotes), `paid`, `created_at`. Amounts are text with two decimals, in the currency of the home."
msgstr "`id`, `project`, `label`, `nature`, `planned`, `committed` (la somme des devis acceptés), `paid`, `created_at`. Les montants sont du texte à deux décimales, dans la devise du logement."

msgid "`project_quotes`"
msgstr "`project_quotes`"

msgid "`id`, `project`, `contractor` (an id or `null`), `amount`, `issued_on`, `valid_until`, `status`, `budget_line` (the line an accepted quote is committed on, else `null`), `note`, `paperless_id`, `paperless_url`, `created_at`."
msgstr "`id`, `project`, `contractor` (un identifiant ou `null`), `amount`, `issued_on`, `valid_until`, `status`, `budget_line` (la ligne sur laquelle un devis accepté est engagé, sinon `null`), `note`, `paperless_id`, `paperless_url`, `created_at`."

msgid "`project_files`"
msgstr "`project_files`"

msgid "`id`, `project`, `quote` (or `null` for a photo of the project), `name`, `content_type`, `is_image`, `size_bytes`, `width`, `height`, `created_at`, and `file`, the path in the archive (`files/projects/<id>.<extension>`, or `null` if the file is missing)."
msgstr "`id`, `project`, `quote` (ou `null` pour une photo du projet), `name`, `content_type`, `is_image`, `size_bytes`, `width`, `height`, `created_at`, et `file`, le chemin dans l'archive (`files/projects/<id>.<extension>`, ou `null` si le fichier manque)."

msgid "`project_tasks`"
msgstr "`project_tasks`"

msgid "`id`, `project`, `task`: the tasks that belong to a project."
msgstr "`id`, `project`, `task` : les tâches qui appartiennent à un projet."

msgid "`project_envelopes`"
msgstr "`project_envelopes`"

msgid "`id`, `year`, `amount`: the annual budget envelope."
msgstr "`id`, `year`, `amount` : l'enveloppe budgétaire annuelle."

msgid "`tasks`"
msgstr "`tasks`"

msgid "`id`, `title`, `room`, `item`, `priority`, `estimated_minutes`, the budgets, `notes`, `procedure`, `assignee`, `contractor` (an id), the repeat rule, `season` (`spring`, `summer`, `autumn`, `winter`, `heating`, `custom` or empty) with `season_start_month` and `season_end_month`, `hide_days_before`."
msgstr "`id`, `title`, `room`, `item`, `priority`, `estimated_minutes`, les budgets, `notes`, `procedure`, `assignee`, `contractor` (un identifiant), la règle de répétition, `season` (`spring`, `summer`, `autumn`, `winter`, `heating`, `custom` ou vide) avec `season_start_month` et `season_end_month`, `hide_days_before`."

msgid "`contractors`"
msgstr "`contractors`"

msgid "`id`, `name`, `trade` (a code of the list, or `other`), `trade_other`, `phone`, `email`, `address`, `note`."
msgstr "`id`, `name`, `trade` (un code de la liste, ou `other`), `trade_other`, `phone`, `email`, `address`, `note`."

msgid "`calendar_feeds`"
msgstr "`calendar_feeds`"

msgid "`id`, `created_at`, `regenerated_at` of each [calendar feed](../guides/calendar.md) of the home. Never the address or its secret, which is not kept; the combined feed of a person belongs to the person, not to a home."
msgstr "`id`, `created_at`, `regenerated_at` de chaque [flux de calendrier](../guides/calendar.md) du logement. Jamais l'adresse ni son secret, qui n'est pas conservé ; le flux combiné d'une personne appartient à la personne, pas à un logement."

msgid "`labels`"
msgstr "`labels`"

msgid "`id`, `kind` (`room`, `item` or `article`), `target` (the id of the room, item or stock item), `code`, `revoked_at`, `created_at` of each QR label. The `code` is the opaque identifier its sticker carries: it is exported for an active label and is `null` for a revoked one, which opens nothing."
msgstr "`id`, `kind` (`room`, `item` ou `article`), `target` (l'identifiant de la pièce, de l'élément ou de l'article), `code`, `revoked_at`, `created_at` de chaque étiquette QR. Le `code` est l'identifiant opaque que porte son autocollant : il est exporté pour une étiquette active et vaut `null` pour une étiquette révoquée, qui n'ouvre rien."

msgid "`reports`"
msgstr "`reports`"

msgid "`id`, `title`, `status`, `place`, `room`, `item` or `stock_item`, `task`, `reporter` (the e-mail address that `members` already holds), `created_at`, `closed_at`, and `file`, the path of the photo in the archive (`files/reports/<id>.<extension>`, or `null`)."
msgstr "`id`, `title`, `status`, `place`, `room`, `item` ou `stock_item`, `task`, `reporter` (l'adresse e-mail que `members` contient déjà), `created_at`, `closed_at`, et `file`, le chemin de la photo dans l'archive (`files/reports/<id>.<extension>`, ou `null`)."

msgid "`files`"
msgstr "`files`"

msgid "`path` and `size` of each file in `files/`."
msgstr "`path` et `size` de chaque fichier de `files/`."

msgid "Photos and the images attached to tasks are exported as they are stored, already stripped of their metadata at upload; the documents attached to tasks are exported as they were received. Thumbnails are not exported, and neither is anything deleted. The archive has no size limit of its own: it is as large as the files of the home (each is limited by `HOUSECAIRN_PHOTO_MAX_BYTES`)."
msgstr "Les photos et les images jointes aux tâches sont exportées telles qu'elles sont stockées, déjà dépouillées de leurs métadonnées au dépôt ; les documents joints aux tâches sont exportés tels qu'ils ont été reçus. Les miniatures ne sont pas exportées, ni rien de ce qui a été supprimé. L'archive n'a pas de plafond de taille propre : elle est aussi grosse que les fichiers du logement (chacun est limité par `HOUSECAIRN_PHOTO_MAX_BYTES`)."

msgid "Each lot that adds data adds its section here and to the archive. The archive holds the home it was made for and nothing of another."
msgstr "Chaque lot qui ajoute des données ajoute sa section ici et dans l'archive. L'archive contient le logement pour lequel elle a été faite, et rien d'un autre."

msgid "Deletion of a home"
msgstr "Suppression d'un logement"

msgid "An owner deletes the home from its page (**Delete this home**): type its exact name. The home and everything in it go for good, for all its members: members, invitations, events, calendar feeds, its audit log and its files; an API token left without a home is revoked. **There is no grace period and no way back**: export first. The audit log of the instance records that a home was deleted, without its name."
msgstr "Un propriétaire supprime le logement depuis sa page (**Supprimer ce logement**) : saisissez son nom exact. Le logement et tout ce qu'il contient disparaissent définitivement, pour tous ses membres : membres, invitations, événements, flux de calendrier, son journal d'audit et ses fichiers ; un jeton d'API resté sans logement est révoqué. **Il n'y a ni délai de grâce ni retour en arrière** : exportez d'abord. Le journal d'audit de l'instance enregistre qu'un logement a été supprimé, sans son nom."

msgid "The photos, the labels of stock items, the photos and quote files of projects, the photos of reports and the files attached to tasks are erased from the disk with the home (photos deleted one by one included). If the disk refuses (permissions, a full or read-only volume), the home is still deleted and the error is logged by `housecairn.files` with the path of the directory (`photos/<home id>`, `attachments/<home id>`, `stock/<home id>`, `projects/<home id>` or `reports/<home id>`): remove that directory by hand."
msgstr "Les photos, les étiquettes des articles du matériel, les photos et fichiers de devis des projets, les photos des signalements et les fichiers joints aux tâches sont effacés du disque avec le logement (les photos supprimées une à une comprises). Si le disque refuse (droits, volume plein ou en lecture seule), le logement est tout de même supprimé et l'erreur est consignée par `housecairn.files` avec le chemin du dossier (`photos/<id du logement>`, `attachments/<id du logement>`, `stock/<id du logement>`, `projects/<id du logement>` ou `reports/<id du logement>`) : supprimez ce dossier à la main."

msgid "Erasure of an account"
msgstr "Effacement d'un compte"

msgid "**Delete my account** (see [Account pages](../screens/account.md)) erases the account, its sign-in methods, devices, API tokens and calendar feeds, the homes where it is the only member, and the invitations to its address. It is refused for the only administrator and for the only owner of a home with other members: hand ownership over, or delete the home, first. The audit log keeps that it happened and no longer says who."
msgstr "**Supprimer mon compte** (voir [Pages du compte](../screens/account.md)) efface le compte, ses méthodes de connexion, ses appareils, ses jetons d'API et ses flux de calendrier, les logements dont il est le seul membre, et les invitations envoyées à son adresse. L'effacement est refusé pour l'unique administrateur et pour l'unique propriétaire d'un logement qui a d'autres membres : transmettez d'abord la propriété, ou supprimez le logement. Le journal d'audit garde la trace de l'opération, sans plus dire qui."

msgid "Backups"
msgstr "Sauvegardes"

msgid "Deleted data stays in backups until they expire: tell people how long you keep them (see [Backup](backup.md))."
msgstr "Les données supprimées restent dans les sauvegardes jusqu'à leur expiration : indiquez aux gens combien de temps vous les conservez (voir [Sauvegarde](backup.md))."

